    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the version-2 owner identity release I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. Version-2 identity derivation (mixes in a fixed `'V2'` tag)** \u2014 every identifier now changes and can never reproduce a v1 value:\n- **Region code inside the identifier** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`): new `identityRegionCode()` = `\"V2\"` + plain region, so the `memberId` prefix becomes e.g. `V2NSW` instead of `NSW`.\n- **`memberId` hash** (`identityHash8`): `\"V2|\"` prepended to the SHA-256 input.\n- **`householdId`** (`householdId`): `\"V2|\"` prepended to the SHA-256 input.\n- **`identityKey`** (`IdentityKeys.identityKey`): `\"V2|\"` prepended, so both the duplicate-detection check and the exposed key move to v2 in lockstep.\n\n**2. `locality`, `timezone`, owner-segment region stay plain** \u2014 `OwnerMapper.locality()` no longer derives the region from the (now V2-tagged) `memberId`; it derives the plain region directly from postcode/city, so `locality` remains `NSW`, `timezone` and the segment's `METRO/REGIONAL` area stay correct. (Removed the now-unused `regionFromMemberId`.)\n\n**3. Response shape** \u2014 in `openapi.yml`, added an `OwnerIdentity` schema and grouped `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` under a nested `identity` object, removed them from the top level, and added a top-level integer `apiVersion` (= 2). `OwnerMapper` populates both via `identity(owner)` and `apiVersion()`.\n\n**4. Audit event schema v2** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent` now emits `\"schemaVersion\":2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the version-2 owner (`STANDARD_METRO` in the run output), alongside the existing fields.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. Verified externals from the run:\n- `memberId=V2NSW27169701686` (v2 region + v2 hash; FY still parses to `27`)\n- audit line: `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW27169701686\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n- `AcceptanceTest` (apiVersion=2, identity grouping, top-level identifiers absent): **passing**.",
