    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`, traced through the actual code path in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` and downstream.\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`); otherwise 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (from the generated `OwnersApi` interface). Declarative constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/'/-)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `title`: `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address`: `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - Failures \u2192 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n\n## Inside the method body (in execution order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header maps to an already-created owner, return that owner as **200 OK** (skips everything below).\n4. **`validateRequiredFields`** \u2014 blank `firstName`/`lastName`/address(either structured or flat)/`city`/`telephone` \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 if postcode present: must be 4 digits, and must fall in the city's region range (Sydney\u21922000-2099, Melbourne\u21923000-3099, Brisbane\u21924000-4099) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n6. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, ignoring `id` and `pets`).\n7. **`applyAddress` / `normalizeAddress`** *(side-effect: normalization)* \u2014 prefers structured lines over flat address; trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET / RD\u2192ROAD / AVE\u2192AVENUE; sets `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, composed `address`.\n8. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n9. **Default + `toBusinessDay`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 null registrationDate defaults to today; then any Sat/Sun/2026-holiday is rolled forward to the next business day.\n10. **`rejectWhenDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 \u2265100 existing owners on that business-day registrationDate \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429). (Loads all owners.)\n11. **`rejectWhenCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 \u226550 existing owners in that city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n12. **`applyHousehold`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets deterministic `householdId` = `\"HH-\" + SHA-256(\"V2|\"+lastName+\"|\"+postcode)[0:12]`.\n13. **`normalizeTelephone` + `validateNationalNumberLength`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 strips separators, assumes `+61` when no `+` (dropping a leading 0), must be `[0-9]{8,15}` with national-number length matching the country code \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400); stores E.164.\n14. **`normalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 blank\u2192null; else trim + lowercase; must match email pattern \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400); disposable domains (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400).\n15. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 computes an identity key (telephone/email/lastName); if any non-deleted owner shares it \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n16. **`memberId`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 generates `<region><FY2><HASH8><Luhn>`, de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix against existing member IDs.\n17. **`countNamesakes`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n18. **`flagPossibleDuplicate` / `findPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, soft-matches on soundex(lastName)+postcode with a different identity key and sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n19. **`clinicService.saveOwner`** *(side-effect: persist)* \u2014 `@Transactional`; new owner (`id == null`) \u2192 `em.persist`. `id` is DB identity-generated. No JPA lifecycle callbacks, entity listeners, or `@CreatedDate`/`@CreatedBy` auditing fire. (Note: the entity's own `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints on `city`/`telephone` are not re-validated on this save path.)\n\n## After save (side-effects)\n\n20. **Idempotency cache write** \u2014 store `key \u2192 owner.getId()` in the in-memory map.\n21. **Audit logging** \u2014 `AUDIT` logger writes a human line plus a structured JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (with an incremented sequence number).\n22. **Notification logging** \u2014 `NOTIFY` logger writes a welcome line.\n23. **Response** \u2014 build `OwnerDto` (with many derived fields: membership level/points, segment, etc.), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n**Not in this path:** no custom `@Constraint` validators, no validation groups, no JPA lifecycle hooks/entity listeners, no JPA auditing, and the service/repository layers do no validation or normalization \u2014 every business rule above is hand-coded in the controller."
